  "result": "All eight tests pass, including the three new namespace tests.\n\n```\n8 passed in 0.08s\n```\n\n**What changed in `kvstore/store.py`:**\n\n- **Schema:** the `kv` table now has an `ns` column, with a composite primary key on namespace plus key. Lookups within a namespace stay indexed, and everything is still one SQLite file.\n- **Existing methods:** `set`, `get`, `delete`, and `keys` take a keyword argument `ns` defaulting to \"default\", and every query filters on it.\n- **New methods:** `count` returns the row count for one namespace. `namespaces` returns the sorted distinct namespace names, so a namespace disappears once its last key is deleted.\n- **Migration:** on open, a legacy table from the first version without an `ns` column is rebuilt in place, moving its rows into the \"default\" namespace. I checked this against a hand-built old-format file and it migrated cleanly with no side files left behind.",
